<newsitem itemid="30615" id="root" date="1996-09-03" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Pentland interim operating profit rises.</title>
<headline>Pentland interim operating profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		1.91		   vs 2.52</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.4		    vs 1.35</p>
<p> Operating profit	 11.4		   vs 10.8</p>
<p> Interest		   0.1		    vs 3.3</p>
<p> Pretax		     11.5		   vs 14.1</p>
<p> Turnover		   412.3		  vs 331.5</p>
<p> Tax			  4.2		    vs 4.9</p>
<p> Net taxed		  7.3		    vs 9.2</p>
<p> Attributable	     6.9		    vs 9.1</p>
<p> Pay date		   November 1 1996</p>
<p>NOTE - Pentland Group Plc is a group with footwear and clothing subsidiaries. Comparative figures have been restated.</p>
<p>The group said its was optimistic that increased distribution capacity from the purchase of additional warehousing facilities would lead to future growth in both sales and operating profit.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
